:name: RPL-UDP across Renode and csim
:description: A CC2538 in Renode is the RPL root; csim's nodes join its DAG and exchange UDP with it.
#
# Two simulators, one radio medium, one RPL DAG. Renode emulates the CC2538
# root and its radio chip; csim emulates the client nodes and the air between
# them. Both run unmodified Contiki-NG with stock CSMA and RPL Lite.
#
# Renode drives the clock and starts csim itself, so this is the only thing
# you run:
#
#   CSIM_CONFIG=$PWD/configs/test-renode-root-rpl.yaml \
#   CSIM_LOG=/tmp/csim.log \
#       renode examples/renode/cc2538-csim-rpl.resc
#   (monitor) start
#
# How the frames cross:
#
#   CC2538 radio ─┐                                    ┌─ nRF52840 (csim)
#                 ├─ Renode wireless ── CsimBridge ──> csim UDGM medium
#   (Renode)     ─┘                        │
#                                 co-simulation window at 0x50100000,
#                                 which also keeps the two clocks in step
#
# The 100 us quantum (frequency x limitBuffer) is the latency budget for an
# 802.15.4 acknowledgement crossing back from csim before the CC2538's driver
# gives up on it -- see docs/design/renode-cosim-plan.md.

$rom ?= @https://dl.antmicro.com/projects/renode/cc2538_rom_dump.bin-s_524288-0c196cdc21b5397f82e0ff42b206d1cc4b6d7522
$fw ?= @firmware/cc2538dk/udp-server-v52.cc2538dk
$launch ?= @tools/csim-renode-launch.sh
$id ?= 2   # must match the dev.renode node's id in CSIM_CONFIG

include @examples/renode/bridge/CsimBridge.cs

# No range function: csim's UDGM decides who hears whom, so Renode's medium
# is a plain hub and propagation is modelled once, not twice.
emulation CreateIEEE802_15_4Medium "wireless"

mach create "cc2538-client"
using sysbus
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/cc2538.repl

# csim itself: the clock master, and the pipe the bridge moves frames through.
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "csim: CoSimulated.CoSimulatedPeripheral @ sysbus <0x50100000, +0x100> { frequency: 1000000; limitBuffer: 100; timeout: 240000; address: \"127.0.0.1\" }"

# The seam between the two media.
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "bridge: Wireless.CsimBridge @ sysbus <0x50000000, +0x20> { csimBase: 0x50100000; pollMicroseconds: 100; channel: 26 }"

connector Connect radio wireless
connector Connect bridge wireless

# CLOCK_STATUS is a constant tag in cc2538.repl; Contiki polls it for the
# oscillator-stable bit, so give it a bit that moves (Renode's own shim).
machine PyDevFromFile @scripts/pydev/rolling-bit.py 0x400D2004 0x4 True "sysctrl"

macro reset
"""
    # IEEE address in flash (0x00 0x12 0x4B is the TI OUI)
    sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x00280028 $id
    sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x0028002C 0x00
    sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x00280030 0xAB
    sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x00280034 0x89
    sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x00280038 0x00
    sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x0028003C 0x4B
    sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x00280040 0x12
    sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x00280044 0x00

    sysbus LoadBinary $rom 0x0
    sysbus LoadELF $fw
    cpu VectorTableOffset `sysbus GetSymbolAddress "vectors"`
"""
runMacro $reset

# Renode starts csim: setting the path is what opens the sockets and launches
# the peer. The scenario comes from CSIM_CONFIG.
csim SimulationFilePathMacOS $launch
csim SimulationFilePathLinux $launch

showAnalyzer sysbus.uart0

echo ""
echo "CC2538 RPL root in Renode; csim's clients join it. 'start' to run."
echo ""
